From bf7b329284790a3d7a96cbf9887b7567eb977e80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:00:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Recolor Post Trip flow to brand palette; fix Detailed card
 and wizard action buttons
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Post Trip's landing screen and the entire "Detailed Trip" wizard
(7 steps + preview) were still on the pre-rebrand palette — most
visibly, the wizard's own Back/Preview/Publish/Next buttons used an
orange-red-pink gradient with no relation to the site's coral/ocean
brand, on what's the primary CTA for the platform's main trip type.

- post-trip.tsx: header gradient and the "Detailed Trip" choice card
  moved from orange/blue/pink to brand/accent. Left the "Quick Trip"
  card and its loading spinner on orange — that's this app's
  established, deliberate color for Quick Trip UI everywhere else,
  not a rebrand miss. The Detailed card now matches accent (ocean),
  consistent with its own loading spinner which was already
  correctly using ceylon-blue.
- PostTripWizard.tsx: Back/Preview/Publish/Next buttons moved off
  orange/red/pink onto brand tokens; "Saved just now" onto success.
- All 7 step components + QuickTripWizard: generic "tips" info boxes
  (blue) onto accent, required-field asterisks (red) onto danger,
  free/success/enabled states (green) onto the success token,
  "Solo Traveler Friendly" sections (pink) onto brand. Left
  QuickTripWizard's orange completely untouched (correct there), and
  left SafetyChecklist.tsx and StepPreview's "Safety Considerations"
  box alone — both use color purely to distinguish sections/severity
  categorically, the same deliberate-variety pattern already kept in
  PreferencesForm.tsx earlier in this rebrand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
